      "claim": "Tetrabenazine has very low oral bioavailability (5.3% fasted), but its low F is driven by extensive first-pass carbonyl reduction of its ketone and a different benzoquinolizidine scaffold; the query lacks this ketone liability, so transferability is low.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
